# F45. Slack has a sheet open when it is docked, so it refuses the size of its space and becomes a tile.
# The sheet closes. Nobody tells Arbor, and nobody should have to close the window to get it back.
quiet
open Safari
open Notes
open Slack 900x700 min 900x700
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
dock 103 beside 102 bottom
expect tile 103
expect hidden 103

# The sheet is gone. For a while nothing changes: Arbor does not pester windows.
min 103 0x0
wait 300
show-all
expect tile 103

# Ten minutes after it refused, the next time anything is laid out, it is asked out of view, and comes back.
wait 300
expect tile 103
show-all
expect visible 103
expect docked 103
expect above 102 103

# A window that really cannot be smaller stays a tile however long it takes, and stays out of view.
open Xcode 1000x800 min 1000x800
dock 104 beside 101 bottom
expect tile 104
wait 3600
show-all
expect tile 104
expect hidden 104
expect visible 101

# Asking by hand needs no waiting.
min 104 0x0
relayout
expect visible 104
